S***.

50
00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:56.400
<i>What's he doing?</i>

51
00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.950
<i>Look at that.</i>

52
00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.540
<i>Get up.</i>

53
00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:15.490
<i>Get up.</i>

54
00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.680
Is it really okay not to say goodbye to the kids?

55
00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.510
Last goodbye? That's so cheesy.

56
00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.210
When you leave. just go coolly.

57
00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:34.690
Aigoo. Mr. Kim Moo Kyung. you're still here.

58
00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:36.530
Oh. yes.

59
00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.900
Good work. Be well.

60
00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.160
Yes. you too.

61
00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.420
Ms. Song Chae Rin. where are you going?

62
00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.080
The meeting starts soon.

63
00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:50.330
I'm okay. Just stay.

64
00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:52.660
I'll just see him off to his car.

65
00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:53.940
What about the meeting?

66
00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:56.660
I'll be right back.

67
00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.350
Geez...

68
00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.860
Why do you insist on seeing me off?

69
00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.800
Do you think I'll get lost?

70
00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.950
Even adults can lose their way.

71
00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.420
Hang in there. Ms. Hong.

72
00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.630
Holding on is winning.

73
00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:27.120
There isn't much time left until Cheol Joo's next trial. right?

74
00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:31.040
I'll keep working on Cheol Joo's trial.

75
00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.600
Just focus on the kids here. Ms. Chae Rin.

76
00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:38.790
And especially the ones who'll go out on site.

77
00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:42.740
The kids loved the woodworking class.

78
00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.480
What will they do now?

79
00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.260
There'll be another good teacher.

80
00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:51.000
I think they already interviewed someone.

81
00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:54.180
- They're quick on things like this.
- I know.

82
00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:00.200
Gosh. Why is it raining so much?

83
00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:05.050
<i>No more unreasonable and unfair dismissals!</i>

84
00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:10.480
<i>We want to keep learning from Mr. Kim Moo Kyung!</i>

85
00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:14.870
<i>No more unreasonable and unfair dismissals!</i>

86
00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:19.750
<i>We want to keep learning from Mr. Kim Moo Kyung!</i>

87
00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:22.470
No more unreasonable...

88
00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.780
Mr. Kim.

89
00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:33.210
You really don't listen to me until the end.

90
00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:36.230
Mr. Kim. are you really leaving like this?

91
00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:37.950
No way.

92
00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.090
I'll fight until the end.

93
00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:43.910
Hey. Fight if you want. but you have to be in class.

94
00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:47.130
You should stop her as her homeroom teacher.

95
00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.240
Who can stop Ji Won?

96
00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.190
You said you'll be the best carpenter in our country.

97
00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.380
Where do you have time to be doing this?

98
00:09:57.810 --> 00:09:58.900
Aigoo.

99
00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.000
Here.

100
00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.350
Bribe.

101
00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.720
It's what I used when I won the National Championship.

102
00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:16.860
If you become famous one day.

103
00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.580
you have to tell them you're my student.

104
00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.020
Mr. Kim.

105
00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:25.200
Come now.

106
00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.490
Fighting.

107
00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:40.790
Get to class.

108
00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.090
Go inside.

109
00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.680
[Moo Kyung]

110
00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.010
<i>We can go home now...</i>

111
00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:13.210
Is the treatment on your injured ankle going well?

112
00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:18.000
Yes. It's much better.

113
00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:21.000
Right. Don't overwork yourself.

114
00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:24.510
You know that even if you don't train. you have to do rehab. right?

115
00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:25.300
Yes.

116
00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:28.190
Carpentry?

117
00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:30.600
Is your life in the new department going well?

118
00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:34.340
Yes.

119
00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.360
Alright. cheer up.

120
00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.060
<i>Here he comes.</i>

121
00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:46.730
<i>Didn't he fall earlier?</i>

122
00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.370
<i>Due to my ankle injury.</i>

123
00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:53.280
<i>I quit taekwondo that I did for 11 years since elementary school.</i>

124
00:11:55.060 --> 00:12:00.200
<i>But the coach and I both knew my ankle was already better.</i>

125
00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:03.600
<i>We don't have much time left. Manage your weight.</i>

126
00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.840
<i>- I just...
- Yes. sir.</i>

127
00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:10.550
<i>didn't have enough talent.</i>

128
00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:12.570
Start the warm-up.

129
00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:15.860
One. two. three. four. five. six...

130
00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.790
<i>Where am I supposed to go now?</i>

131
00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:43.540
What's this?

132
00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:44.930
Seriously.

133
00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:01.830
[Anniversary of Gyeong Min's death D-1]

134
00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:07.300
Anyway. Jin Ji Won. you're amazing.

135
00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.680
You were the last one standing.

136
00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.200
Sorry. we couldn't be with you until the end.

137
00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.660
It's okay.

138
00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:15.660
You'll both be blacklisted by the school.

139
00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:18.380
Only you would look out for us.

140
00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:19.740
That's right.

141
00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:20.900
- Oh!
- What? Why?

142
00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:23.310
- I'm hungry.
- You are?

143
00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:24.970
Should we go to the snack store?

144
00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.930
A puppy lives inside my stomach...

145
00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:29.650
- A puppy lives in her stomach.
- It rumbles...

146
00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.280
Where are you going?

147
00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.260
Hey. Gong Ki Joon.

148
00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.250
Where are you going?

149
00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:53.680
Home.

150
00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.490
Looks like you're skipping school.

151
00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.410
You told me to lay off.

152
00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.030
What's up with him?

153
00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:20.970
♫ <i>Not knowing makes me want to know more</i> ♫

154
00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:31.600
♫ <i>Liking you sometimes makes me more anxious</i> ♫

155
00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:41.500
♫ <i>I want to see the glimmering sea</i> ♫

156
00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:52.700
[Cha Gyeong Min]
♫ <i>On my way there. I miss you more</i> ♫

157
00:14:55.750 --> 00:15:05.810
♫ <i>Another day passes by</i> ♫

158
00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.250
How are you?

159
00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:13.630
I quit taekwondo.

160
00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:20.820
♫ <i>I think of you</i> ♫

161
00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:21.970
Hey.

162
00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:24.520
What do I do now?

163
00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:32.800
♫ <i>And then. in one moment</i> ♫

164
00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:35.730
♫ <i>The heart that aches</i> ♫

165
00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.440
I miss you.

166
00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:09.700
♫ <i>Will you. will you remember me?</i> ♫

167
00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:15.300
♫ <i>Me. a child who looked at you</i> ♫

168
00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:18.800
♫ <i>who looked at you</i> ♫

169
00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:25.980
♫ <i>I think of you</i> ♫

170
00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:31.130
♫ <i>That's love</i> ♫

171
00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:39.600
♫ <i>And then. suddenly I feel that way again</i> ♫

172
00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:42.680
I'll be going now.

173
00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:50.070
♫ <i>Without knowing. I want to know your heart</i> ♫

174
00:16:53.450 --> 00:17:00.800
♫ <i>My heart has grown overnight</i> ♫

175
00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:11.280
♫ <i>I want to see the sparkling night sky</i> ♫

176
00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:22.280
♫ <i>I miss you more on these strange roads</i> ♫

177
00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:47.860
Grandpa.

178
00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:50.580
Oh. welcome.

179
00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:55.070
What are you doing here? You have back pain.

180
00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:56.300
Yeah...

181
00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:57.810
You're using this space again?

182
00:17:57.810 --> 00:17:59.930
I'm trying to clean things up in advance.

183
00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:01.900
Why suddenly?

184
00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:09.310
Was the house auctioned off?

185
00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:10.500
Yeah.

186
00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:17.430
The bids fell through for so long. It was about time it succeeded.

187
00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:25.190
Just leave it. I'll do it.

188
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.700
Alright.

189
00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:41.290
I'll earn a lot of money and buy this house back for you.

190
00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:46.770
I should live long to see my grandson become rich.

191
00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.130
It won't take that long.

192
00:18:57.640 --> 00:18:59.830
<i>I have a lot of time.</i>

193
00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:02.840
<i>And I need money.</i>

194
00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:36.130
Anyway. there were a lot of trials and errors in the beginning.

195
00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:38.410
It really couldn't be helped.

196
00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:40.240
So the important thing is that

197
00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:43.550
I realized. 'I'm becoming a professional in my field.'

198
00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:46.950
That thought made me feel really proud.

199
00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:51.230
At the center was the Nulji High School architectural design department and the apprenticeship class.

200
00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:54.850
I'm utilizing a lot that I learned at school in the field now.

201
00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:57.970
That's all I have to say today. Not sure if it was helpful.

202
00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:00.950
Now. ask away any questions you have.

203
00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:02.740
Yes?

204
00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:07.340
So. did you become employed full-time right after you took the apprenticeship class and graduated?

205
00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:08.340
Yes.

206
00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:12.520
For me. I signed a contract with the company in 11th grade.

207
00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.420
I worked and studied at the same time.

208
00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:18.500
and got hired full-time before graduating. and I'm still working there.

209
00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:20.900
Yes?

210
00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:24.480
Wouldn't it still be better to work after going to college?

211
00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:26.570
Did you regret it or anything?

212
00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.250
I'm not sure.

213
00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:30.720
Rather than going to college without any thought.

214
00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:33.580
wouldn't it be more efficient to work at a company

215
00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:36.260
and go when you think you need to?

216
00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:38.160
You all know P-TECH. right?

217
00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:41.190
<i>Yes. we know.</i>

218
00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.270
P-TECH?

219
00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:46.210
I'm using that to take college classes on the weekends.

220
00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:50.680
Of course. there is no College Scholastic Ability Test or tuition.

221
00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:53.840
Yes?

222
00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:58.070
But it's hard enough for us to earn our certificates now.

223
00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:00.240
Isn't apprenticeship too much?

224
00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:05.900
Right. working an apprenticeship can be more work than just a regular curriculum.

225
00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:11.080
But think about it.

226
00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:15.880
You're going on-site to learn while still attending school

227
00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:22.300
and you get a monthly salary deposited every month to your bank accounts.

228
00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.770
Huh? Isn't this really appealing?

229
00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:27.960
You won't start your 20s with a debt.

230
00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:30.540
You'll start it with savings.

231
00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:37.140
Yes?

232
00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:39.800
How much is the monthly salary?

233
00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:41.640
Monthly salary...

234
00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:45.080
Monthly salary...

235
00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:47.400
Every company is different.

236
00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:50.650
But I guarantee you it's more than the minimum wage.

237
00:21:50.650 --> 00:21:52.970
Including the four national insurances.

238
00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:58.530
Yes?

239
00:21:58.530 --> 00:21:59.660
So...

240
00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:02.090
what's an apprenticeship?

241
00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:06.660
Huh?

242
00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:13.120
Hey.

243
00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:14.560
Be quiet.

244
00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:16.420
Why?

245
00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:19.250
Just be quiet.

246
00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:22.400
Alright. no more questions?

247
00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.470
That's about it for the talk with your sunbae.

248
00:22:24.470 --> 00:22:27.010
They're recruiting one more apprentice

249
00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:29.610
at Sang Rim Housing. where Jung Min works.

250
00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:31.610
- so if anyone's interested-
- Me.

251
00:22:31.610 --> 00:22:33.290
I get to go on-site. right?

252
00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:34.580
I want to do it.

253
00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:38.630
Oh. you.

254
00:22:38.630 --> 00:22:40.730
Ji Won. Yes.

255
00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:43.510
Alright. Anyone else?

256
00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:52.000
Me too.

257
00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:54.580
You too?

258
00:22:54.580 --> 00:22:55.910
Why-oh. okay.

259
00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:58.250
Okay.

260
00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:00.390
What are you doing?

261
00:23:00.390 --> 00:23:02.700
Put your hand down.

262
00:23:02.700 --> 00:23:04.420
Put your hand down.

263
00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:08.970
Hey. Gong Ki Joon.

264
00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:14.130
Why are you interested in an apprenticeship?

265
00:23:14.130 --> 00:23:15.810
You don't even know what it is.

266
00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:16.940
Why?

267
00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:18.310
Am I not allowed?

268
00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:19.930
No. but...

269
00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:23.410
You never even took the major classes properly while doing taekwondo.

270
00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:26.140
They said they'd teach me.

271
00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:28.880
You're doing this on purpose. right?

272
00:23:32.060 --> 00:23:33.490
What are you talking about?

273
00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:47.490
- Wow.
- Whoa.

274
00:23:48.370 --> 00:23:51.710
- I say yes.
- I bet 500 won that they used to date.

275
00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:55.000
That can't be right.

276
00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:59.650
The whole class saw Jin Ji Won beating up Gong Ki Joon in fourth grade.

277
00:23:59.650 --> 00:24:03.240
Ki Joon got a double nosebleed. It was a whole mess.

278
00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:05.560
Hey. that was then.

279
00:24:05.560 --> 00:24:08.030
Why would Ki Joon suddenly apply to the apprenticeship?

280
00:24:11.110 --> 00:24:13.230
Because he wanted to work with Ji Won?

281
00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:15.820
No. I applied to earn money.

282
00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:17.000
<i>Yes.</i>

283
00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:19.690
Even in elementary school. there was a rumor they were dating.

284
00:24:19.690 --> 00:24:21.710
Please focus on my skills. not those rumors.

285
00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:24.200
I dreamed of becoming a carpenter since elementary school

286
00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:26.140
and it hasn't changed at all.

287
00:24:26.140 --> 00:24:27.870
They were supposed to select one.

288
00:24:27.870 --> 00:24:31.010
This isn't romance. It's a 'screw-you.'

289
00:24:31.010 --> 00:24:33.760
I did it for the money. not my dream.

290
00:24:33.760 --> 00:24:36.260
I'm prepared to endure.

291
00:24:40.870 --> 00:24:43.450
Ho Sung. do you know anything?

292
00:24:43.450 --> 00:24:45.800
You were close with them since elementary school.

293
00:24:45.800 --> 00:24:49.280
Ki Joon and Ji Won. are they enemies or lovers?

294
00:24:56.420 --> 00:24:57.610
It's hard to tell.

295
00:24:57.610 --> 00:24:58.940
Gosh...

296
00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:05.400
What's going on? You guys were badmouthing me. huh?

297
00:25:05.480 --> 00:25:07.610
Yeah. Hold on a second.

298
00:25:07.610 --> 00:25:09.270
Seriously.

299
00:25:09.270 --> 00:25:11.480
How did the apprenticeship with Sang Rim go?

300
00:25:11.480 --> 00:25:12.640
Huh?

301
00:25:28.360 --> 00:25:31.250
- They're both good.
- Yes.

302
00:25:32.600 --> 00:25:37.180
Well. you only have to meet the bare minimum for the major grades.

303
00:25:37.180 --> 00:25:41.080
For now. you should both prepare to interview with Sang Rim.

304
00:25:42.920 --> 00:25:47.440
Ki Joon. all you did was sports. huh?

305
00:25:49.760 --> 00:25:52.270
How about we just go with Ji Won?

306
00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:13.960
Stop talking about that!

307
00:26:13.960 --> 00:26:15.780
- I'm hungry. Hungry!
- Hear me out!

308
00:26:15.780 --> 00:26:18.290
Come on!

309
00:26:18.290 --> 00:26:19.510
I'm hungry!

310
00:26:19.510 --> 00:26:22.110
- When is Min Seo coming?
- I think that's her.

311
00:26:22.110 --> 00:26:23.470
Oh. there's Min Seo!

312
00:26:23.470 --> 00:26:26.540
- Min Seo!
- Min Seo!

313
00:26:26.540 --> 00:26:28.800
